Noto Sans Syriac Western is an unmodulated (sans serif) Serto design
for texts in the Middle Eastern Syriac script. It is the design used
for West Syriac, for Turoyo, and for Garshuni, which is Arabic
written with Syriac characters. It also covers Latin characters.

This package installs the complete upstream font set, not the reduced
Google Fonts subset, under /usr/share/fonts/TTF:

  NotoSansSyriacWestern-Thin.ttf, NotoSansSyriacWestern-Regular.ttf,
  NotoSansSyriacWestern-Black.ttf, and the variable font
  NotoSansSyriacWestern[wght].ttf.

The static fonts cover the Thin, Regular, and Black weights. The
variable font carries a weight axis from Thin to Black, but the upstream
3.001 release registers only Thin, Regular, and Black as named weights.
Intermediate weights are therefore not offered by name.

The fonts are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The
license text is in /usr/doc/ttf-noto-sans-syriac-western-<version>/.
